@startuml Task-Creation-Notification-Sequence
title Task Creation with Kafka and FCM Notification Flow

actor "HR Manager" as HR
participant "Client App" as Client
participant "TasksController" as TaskCtrl
participant "TasksService" as TaskSvc
participant "MongoDB" as DB
participant "Kafka\nProducer" as Kafka
participant "Kafka Topic\n(task.created)" as Topic
participant "Golang\nNotification\nService" as Golang
participant "PostgreSQL" as PG
participant "FCM Server" as FCM
participant "Mobile App\n(Employee)" as Mobile
actor "Employee" as Employee

== Task Creation ==

HR -> Client: Create new task\n(assign to employee)
Client -> TaskCtrl: POST /tasks\n{title, description, assigneeId, deadline}

activate TaskCtrl
TaskCtrl -> TaskSvc: create(createTaskDto, currentUser)
activate TaskSvc

' Create task in database
TaskSvc -> TaskSvc: Validate task data
TaskSvc -> DB: Insert task document
activate DB
DB --> TaskSvc: Task created with _id
deactivate DB

' Publish event to Kafka
TaskSvc -> Kafka: Publish task.created event
activate Kafka

note right of Kafka
  Event payload:
  {
    "eventType": "task.created",
    "taskId": "...",
    "assigneeId": "...",
    "title": "...",
    "description": "...",
    "deadline": "...",
    "createdBy": "...",
    "timestamp": "..."
  }
end note

Kafka -> Topic: Send message
activate Topic
Topic --> Kafka: Acknowledged
deactivate Topic
Kafka --> TaskSvc: Event published
deactivate Kafka

TaskSvc --> TaskCtrl: Created task
deactivate TaskSvc

TaskCtrl --> Client: 201 Created\n{task data}
deactivate TaskCtrl

Client --> HR: Task created successfully

== Golang Service Consumes Event ==

Topic -> Golang: Kafka message received
activate Golang

Golang -> Golang: Parse event payload
Golang -> Golang: Extract assigneeId

' Get employee FCM token from MongoDB via API or cache
Golang -> Golang: Lookup FCM token\nfor assigneeId

Golang -> Golang: Build notification payload
note right of Golang
  Notification payload:
  {
    "title": "New Task Assigned",
    "body": "You have a new task: {title}",
    "data": {
      "taskId": "...",
      "type": "task_created",
      "deadline": "..."
    }
  }
end note

' Send FCM notification
Golang -> FCM: Send push notification\n(using Firebase Admin SDK)
activate FCM

FCM -> FCM: Validate FCM token
FCM -> Mobile: Push notification
activate Mobile

Mobile -> Mobile: Receive notification\n(foreground/background/quit)

Mobile -> Mobile: Display notification
Mobile --> Employee: Show notification:\n"New Task Assigned"
deactivate Mobile

FCM --> Golang: Send result\n{messageId, success: true}
deactivate FCM

' Store notification history in PostgreSQL
Golang -> PG: INSERT INTO notifications\n(user_id, type, payload, status, sent_at)
activate PG
PG --> Golang: Notification record saved
deactivate PG

Golang -> Topic: Acknowledge message
deactivate Golang

== Employee Opens Notification ==

Employee -> Mobile: Tap notification
activate Mobile

Mobile -> Client: Navigate to task detail
Mobile -> TaskCtrl: GET /tasks/:id
activate TaskCtrl

TaskCtrl -> TaskSvc: findOne(taskId)
activate TaskSvc
TaskSvc -> DB: Find task by ID
activate DB
DB --> TaskSvc: Task details
deactivate DB
TaskSvc --> TaskCtrl: Task data
deactivate TaskSvc

TaskCtrl --> Mobile: 200 OK\n{task details}
deactivate TaskCtrl

Mobile -> Mobile: Display task details
Mobile --> Employee: Show task:\ntitle, description, deadline
deactivate Mobile

== Error Handling ==

alt FCM Token Invalid
  Golang -> FCM: Send notification
  activate FCM
  FCM --> Golang: Error: Invalid token
  deactivate FCM
  
  Golang -> PG: INSERT notification\n(status: failed, error: invalid_token)
  activate PG
  PG --> Golang: Saved
  deactivate PG
  
  Golang -> Golang: Log error
  note right of Golang
    Handle gracefully:
    - Log the error
    - Mark token as invalid
    - Optionally retry or
      notify via alternative channel
  end note
end

note bottom of Topic
  Kafka ensures:
  - Reliable message delivery
  - Decoupling of services
  - Scalability
  - Event replay capability
end note

note bottom of PG
  Notification history provides:
  - Audit trail
  - Delivery status tracking
  - Analytics data
  - Troubleshooting
end note

@enduml
